  o Directory authority changes:
    - Directory authorities now list the protocol capabilities "DESC_NO_TAP"
      and "MICRODESC_NO_TAP" as required for clients and relays.
      This changes will allow us to remove TAP keys from onion desciptors
      and microdescriptors, saving a great deal of directory bandwidth.
      Because of this change, Tor versions 0.4.8 and earlier will no longer
      work on the network.
    - Directory authorities now list the protocol capabilities
      "RELAY_NEGOTIATE_SUBPROTO" and "RELAY_CRYPT_CGO" as required for relays.
      This change will allow clients to assume that all relays support
      Counter Galois Onion encryption, and use it even for relays not
      currently listed in the consensus.
